1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:07,310
Give a robot the instruction to move a cup onto a coaster, and several decisions appear before the hand moves.
让机器人把杯子放到杯垫上，在手开始运动之前，就已经出现了多个决策问题。

2
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:16,670
A world model might generate training examples, suggest a visual plan, help evaluate candidate actions, or support joint learning of video and behavior.
世界模型可以生成训练样本、提出视觉计划、帮助评估候选动作，或者支持视频与行为的联合学习。

3
00:00:17,210 --> 00:00:21,670
These are different positions in the system, with different inputs and different responsibilities.
它们处在系统的不同位置，接收不同输入，也承担不同职责。

4
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:28,510
We will connect each position to a concrete paper, then build a clearly labeled engineering example for our cup task.
我们把这些位置对应到具体论文，再为杯子任务构建明确标注的工程示例。

5
00:00:29,053 --> 00:00:37,813
A vision-language-action policy receives observations and a task description, then outputs commands in a particular robot interface.
视觉语言动作策略接收观测与任务描述，再输出某种机器人接口下的指令。

6
00:00:38,393 --> 00:00:42,278
A generated video instead describes a possible sequence of appearances.
生成视频描述的则是一串可能出现的画面。

7
00:00:42,293 --> 00:00:50,153
To connect them, specify the robot embodiment, coordinate frame, units, time step, and which signals are observed or predicted.
要连接两者，就必须明确机器人形态、坐标系、单位、时间步，以及哪些信号被观察、哪些被预测。

8
00:00:50,593 --> 00:00:56,238
A cup moving right in image space could result from object motion, camera motion, or a different viewpoint.
图像中的杯子向右移动，可能来自物体运动、相机运动，或者视角变化。

9
00:00:56,253 --> 00:01:02,569
Without a grounded action interface, visual progress does not uniquely determine the command that caused it.
缺少有依据的动作接口，视觉进展并不能唯一决定造成变化的指令。

10
00:01:03,019 --> 00:01:10,899
UniPi starts from the current image and a language instruction, and generates a video describing a possible task trajectory.
UniPi 从当前图像与语言指令出发，生成描述可能任务轨迹的视频。

11
00:01:11,439 --> 00:01:16,939
An inverse-dynamics model then converts visual transitions into actions for the target environment.
逆动力学模型再把视觉转移转成目标环境里的动作。

12
00:01:17,539 --> 00:01:26,099
Follow the original pipeline carefully: the video generator proposes what should happen, while the inverse model estimates how to produce that change.
仔细看原流程图：视频生成器提出应该发生什么，逆模型估计怎样实现这种变化。

13
00:01:26,599 --> 00:01:31,464
This separates a visual planning interface from the embodiment-specific control interface.
这样，视觉规划接口与具体机器人形态的控制接口被分开。

14
00:01:31,479 --> 00:01:38,379
It also creates two possible failure points: an impossible visual plan or an incorrect action inferred from it.
同时也带来两个失败位置：视觉计划本身不可实现，或者由它推断的动作错误。

15
00:01:38,907 --> 00:01:47,927
UniPi discusses applying its components in a model-predictive-control loop, but explicitly describes its reported experiments as open-loop.
UniPi 讨论了把组件放进模型预测控制循环，但明确把报告中的实验描述为开环。

16
00:01:48,387 --> 00:01:51,787
That distinction matters when the cup slips halfway through the plan.
当杯子在计划执行到一半时滑动，这个区别就非常重要。

17
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:57,107
An open-loop execution does not automatically regenerate the plan from the changed scene.
开环执行不会自动根据变化后的场景重新生成计划。

18
00:01:57,607 --> 00:02:06,592
Also distinguish video evaluation from robot evaluation: a classifier recognizing success in a generated final frame measures that generated video.
还要区分视频评估与机器人评估：分类器在生成末帧中识别成功，测量的是那段生成视频。

19
00:02:06,607 --> 00:02:10,927
It is not, by itself, a measured rate of physically completed robot tasks.
这本身并不是物理机器人实际完成任务的成功率。

20
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:18,820
DreamGen places video generation before policy training rather than requiring the generator to run at every control step.
DreamGen 把视频生成放在策略训练之前，而不是要求生成器在每个控制步运行。

21
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:26,680
Its pipeline first adapts a video world model to the target robot, then generates trajectories from initial images and instructions.
流程先让视频世界模型适配目标机器人，再根据起始图像与指令生成轨迹。

22
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:33,020
A latent-action model or inverse-dynamics model supplies pseudo-actions for the generated visual transitions.
潜在动作模型或逆动力学模型为生成的视觉转移补上伪动作。

23
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:37,005
The resulting examples are used to train a downstream robot policy.
这些样本用于训练下游机器人策略。

24
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:43,940
The useful question is whether those synthetic examples improve real execution under the reported data and evaluation conditions.
真正有用的问题是：在报告的数据与评估条件下，这些合成样本是否改善真实执行。

25
00:02:44,646 --> 00:02:51,146
Suppose a generated trajectory shows the cup rising, but the fingers never form a stable contact.
假设生成轨迹显示杯子升起，但手指从未形成稳定接触。

26
00:02:51,426 --> 00:02:58,586
An inverse model may still output a plausible-looking command sequence, because it must explain the visual transition it was given.
逆模型仍可能输出看起来合理的指令序列，因为它需要解释给定的视觉转移。

27
00:02:58,986 --> 00:03:02,866
Those labels were inferred; they were not measured during the imagined event.
这些标签是推断出来的，并不是在那个想象事件中测量到的。

28
00:03:03,326 --> 00:03:09,631
Synthetic-data quality therefore needs checks for instruction alignment, action plausibility, and downstream usefulness.
因此，合成数据质量需要检查指令一致性、动作合理性，以及下游是否真正受益。

29
00:03:09,646 --> 00:03:19,406
DreamGen's robot adaptation also uses collected robot data, so synthetic augmentation should not be described as learning physical control from no robot experience.
DreamGen 的机器人适配也使用采集的机器人数据，所以合成增强不能被描述为没有机器人经验就学会物理控制。

30
00:03:20,194 --> 00:03:25,974
GR-2 connects video prediction and action generation inside a shared learning system.
GR-2 在同一学习系统中连接视频预测与动作生成。

31
00:03:26,534 --> 00:03:31,874
It first learns from large-scale video, then adapts using robot trajectories with actions.
它先从大规模视频学习，再使用带动作的机器人轨迹适配。

32
00:03:32,414 --> 00:03:39,074
In the original method, video and action predictions are parallel outputs, with a conditional variational action component.
在原方法中，视频与动作是并行输出，动作分支包含条件变分组件。

33
00:03:39,614 --> 00:03:44,214
This is different from searching many imagined futures online and choosing the best trajectory.
这与在线搜索许多想象未来、再选最优轨迹不同。

34
00:03:44,454 --> 00:03:53,734
And the robot's low-level controller frequency should not be reported as the neural model's decision frequency; those numbers belong to different layers of the execution stack.
机器人的底层控制频率也不能写成神经模型的决策频率；它们属于执行系统的不同层。

35
00:03:54,303 --> 00:04:01,563
The original WorldVLA studies an autoregressive system that jointly models visual information and robot actions.
原版 WorldVLA 研究自回归系统，联合建模视觉信息与机器人动作。

36
00:04:02,503 --> 00:04:09,343
Action prediction can benefit from understanding visual consequences, while action information can help predict scene changes.
动作预测可以从理解视觉后果中受益，动作信息也可以帮助预测场景变化。

37
00:04:09,623 --> 00:04:16,583
Its attention design addresses dependencies within predicted action sequences, including the risk of compounding action errors.
它的注意力设计处理预测动作序列内部的依赖，包括动作误差累积的风险。

38
00:04:17,183 --> 00:04:21,628
Read this as a particular joint-training architecture with its reported LIBERO evaluation.
应把它理解为一种具体的联合训练架构，并结合论文报告的 LIBERO 评估来读。

39
00:04:21,643 --> 00:04:31,883
The presence of a world-modeling objective does not establish that deployment performs explicit online MPC or that the system has already solved arbitrary physical manipulation.
加入世界建模目标，并不能证明部署时执行了显式在线 MPC，也不能证明它已经解决任意真实操作任务。

40
00:04:32,668 --> 00:04:38,368
Now build an engineering example, rather than attributing a new experiment to those papers.
现在构建一个工程示例，而不是把新实验归到上述论文名下。

41
00:04:38,988 --> 00:04:45,868
A VLA proposes several candidate actions for moving the cup, and an action-conditioned model predicts their consequences.
VLA 为移动杯子提出多个候选动作，动作条件模型预测它们的后果。

42
00:04:46,568 --> 00:04:52,948
A task score ranks candidates, while the controller executes only the selected first step and observes again.
任务评分排序候选，控制器只执行选中的第一步，然后重新观察。

43
00:04:53,568 --> 00:05:01,153
V-JEPA 2-AC provides a concrete example of feature-space planning, although it is not this exact VLA-candidate architecture.
V-JEPA 2-AC 提供了特征空间规划的具体例子，但它不是这里完全相同的 VLA 候选架构。

44
00:05:01,168 --> 00:05:07,568
Adding a model should be justified by measured improvement over the same policy without that extra computation.
增加模型，需要用实测改进来证明价值，并与没有额外计算的同一策略比较。

45
00:05:08,317 --> 00:05:13,317
A model and a policy trained on similar data may share the same blind spot.
在相似数据上训练的模型与策略，可能共享同一个盲点。

46
00:05:13,857 --> 00:05:19,597
Both might treat a transparent cup as empty space or miss an unstable contact behind the fingers.
两者都可能把透明杯子当成空处，或者漏掉手指背后的不稳定接触。

47
00:05:20,097 --> 00:05:28,162
A high predicted reward therefore cannot replace joint limits, collision checks, controller limits, or direct measurements needed by the application.
因此，高预测奖励不能替代应用所需的关节限制、碰撞检查、控制器约束或直接测量。

48
00:05:28,177 --> 00:05:33,702
Some of those checks use geometry or known robot mechanics rather than the learned predictor.
其中一些检查依靠几何或已知机器人机构，而不是学习预测器。

49
00:05:33,717 --> 00:05:41,177
Treat model confidence as one signal to evaluate, with explicit fallback behavior when observation and prediction disagree.
应把模型置信度当成需要评估的一种信号，并明确观测与预测不一致时的退回行为。

50
00:05:41,767 --> 00:05:49,007
Our cup example now has a complete loop: observe, estimate, propose, predict, choose, execute, and observe again.
现在杯子例子拥有完整循环：观察、估计、提议、预测、选择、执行，再次观察。

51
00:05:49,327 --> 00:05:54,907
But each stage consumes time, and the robot continues moving while some computations are running.
但每个阶段都消耗时间，而部分计算运行时机器人仍在运动。

52
00:05:55,267 --> 00:06:00,687
A prediction based on an old frame can become stale before its selected action reaches the controller.
基于旧画面的预测，在所选动作到达控制器之前就可能过时。

53
00:06:01,067 --> 00:06:07,272
Measure end-to-end latency, synchronize timestamps, and define how action chunks are interrupted or refreshed.
需要测量端到端延迟，同步时间戳，并定义动作块如何中断或更新。

54
00:06:07,287 --> 00:06:13,287
The right planning horizon depends on those timings and on how rapidly the relevant contacts can change.
合适的规划长度取决于这些时序，也取决于相关接触变化得有多快。

55
00:06:13,894 --> 00:06:20,214
Moving a visible object across free space is different from predicting what happens when fingers make contact.
预测可见物体在自由空间中移动，与预测手指接触后的情况不同。

56
00:06:20,834 --> 00:06:26,594
A small pose error can change whether a finger touches the rim, pushes the cup, or misses it entirely.
很小的位姿误差，就可能改变手指是碰到杯沿、推动杯子，还是完全错过。

57
00:06:27,214 --> 00:06:32,154
Friction, compliance, and unseen support conditions then affect whether the object lifts or slips.
摩擦、柔顺性与看不见的支撑条件，随后影响物体是升起还是滑落。

58
00:06:32,654 --> 00:06:37,079
A visually smooth prediction may hide these discontinuities instead of resolving them.
视觉平滑的预测，可能掩盖这些突变，而不是解决它们。

59
00:06:37,094 --> 00:06:46,094
For this application, evaluate contact transitions and complete pick-and-place outcomes, not only image resemblance or an attractive generated grasp.
对这种应用，应评估接触转换与完整抓放结果，而不只是图像相似度或好看的生成抓握。

60
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:54,020
If deployment compute is tight, synthetic-data generation can move expensive video modeling into an offline stage.
如果部署算力紧张，合成数据可以把昂贵的视频建模移到离线阶段。

61
00:06:54,400 --> 00:07:00,980
If the task has a clear goal image and calibrated actions, online feature-space planning may be a candidate to test.
如果任务有清楚的目标图像与校准动作，可以测试在线特征空间规划。

62
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:07,880
If action labels and video trajectories are available, joint learning can share useful representations across objectives.
如果动作标签与视频轨迹都可用，联合学习可以让不同目标共享有用表示。

63
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:11,925
These are conditional design choices, not a ranking of paper names.
这些是带条件的设计选择，而不是论文名字的排名。

64
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:18,660
Choose by the available data, sensor interface, control deadline, and the failure that the added model is meant to reduce.
应根据可用数据、传感器接口、控制时限，以及希望新增模型减少哪类失败来选择。

65
00:07:19,266 --> 00:07:23,906
A hybrid system is only as convincing as the evidence connecting its stages.
混合系统是否可信，取决于连接各阶段的证据。

66
00:07:24,306 --> 00:07:29,766
For generated data, check whether inferred labels improve an independently evaluated policy.
对于生成数据，要检查推断标签是否改善了独立评估的策略。

67
00:07:30,206 --> 00:07:38,906
For visual plans, check whether actions realize them; for runtime evaluation, check whether the chosen action improves the real task under the same budget.
对于视觉计划，要检查动作是否实现计划；对于运行时评估，要在相同预算下检查所选动作是否改善真实任务。

68
00:07:39,246 --> 00:07:44,471
Keep video quality, action prediction, and completed physical outcomes as separate measurements.
把视频质量、动作预测与完整物理结果分开测量。

69
00:07:44,486 --> 00:07:52,706
The final chapter turns these distinctions into a practical evaluation protocol that preserves failures and makes comparisons interpretable.
最后一章把这些区别转成实际评测协议，保留失败，并让比较能够被正确解读。
